  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA VAT-registered exporter that sells 100% of its goods abroad can obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT. This is provided under the provisions of the NIRC that allow for the refund of input VAT on zero-rated sales.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor a VAT-registered exporter, this provision allows for the recovery of input VAT, which can significantly enhance liquidity. The exporter must ensure proper documentation and compliance with the requirements set forth by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) to successfully claim the refund or credit. This includes maintaining accurate records of sales and purchases, as well as filing the necessary claims within the prescribed periods.",
